Target host pidfd compatibility check (2026-09-12)

Host: marslab-server
Kernel: 6.8.0-137-generic

Cross-compiled Linux test binaries executed on target:
- cmd/vela-validation-runtime-launcher: TestRecvFrameStopsWhenContextIsCanceled PASS; TestRecvFrameReturnsEOFOnPeerClose PASS.
- internal/runtimechannel: TestPollLivePIDFDActualProcessExit PASS; TestPollLivePIDFDProcessHelper PASS; TestSameLiveProcessReportsPidfdFilesystem PASS; TestSameLiveProcessRejectsDifferentLegacyPIDFD PASS.

The target does not expose pidfs (pidfd f_type is 0x09041934, while PID_FS_MAGIC is 0x50494446). pidfd_open returns anon_inode:[pidfd]. The implementation validates the kernel fd and uses /proc/self/fdinfo Pid/NSpid only when that identity is visible and comparable. In a nested PID namespace the same kernel reports Pid/NSpid as 0; that handle remains usable for liveness/signalling but SameLiveProcess returns ErrPIDFDIdentityUnavailable and requires a trusted host-side identity broker. No numeric PID is reacquired. A kernel without pidfd_open or without a broker for an invisible legacy pidfd remains fail-closed.
